# A long flythrough under ray tracing (reports/render-features/2026-11-08-rt-revisit/step-default.md, «Приёмка»):
# the route of streaming-flythrough, market -> harbour -> forest and back, ten laps at 10 m/s on the normal clock
# (about 2 min a lap), so chunks and their landscape BLAS come and go many times. Each lap is a perf segment
# `streaming-flythrough/lap-N` that ends in the market after the streaming settles: its `streaming_end` event carries
# the probe's GPU bytes. The `render: rt landscape` / `render: rt scene` lines and those events exist only in the
# frame-profile build, which scripts/ryzen.sh makes for a scenario named streaming-flythrough; so run a copy of this
# file under that name (the flythrough's own report then fails: it wants the passes run and fly):
#   mkdir -p /tmp/soak && cp scripts/bench/rt-default-soak.bench /tmp/soak/streaming-flythrough.bench
#   BENCH_HOST=ryzen RYZEN_MAX=60m scripts/bench.sh /tmp/soak/streaming-flythrough.bench
# and compare the process's video memory (nvidia-smi) and the ray scene's lines at the laps' ends with lap 1.
# @timeout 3600
seed 73030
cheat god
world-check NEWWORLD.ZEN
set time 12 0
cadence normal
overlay off
ui off
view full
cam lift off
watch player
cam look 120
cam world 700 280 180
goto NW_CITY_MERCHANT_TRADE_04
wait 10000
streaming wait
mark lap-0
perf sample streaming-flythrough/lap-1
route 1000 NW_CITY_MERCHANT_TRADE_04 NW_CITY_HABOUR_BENCH_01 NW_FOREST_PATH_16
streaming wait
route 1000 NW_FOREST_PATH_16 NW_CITY_HABOUR_BENCH_01 NW_CITY_MERCHANT_TRADE_04
streaming wait
wait 5000
perf stop
mark lap-1
perf sample streaming-flythrough/lap-2
route 1000 NW_CITY_MERCHANT_TRADE_04 NW_CITY_HABOUR_BENCH_01 NW_FOREST_PATH_16
streaming wait
route 1000 NW_FOREST_PATH_16 NW_CITY_HABOUR_BENCH_01 NW_CITY_MERCHANT_TRADE_04
streaming wait
wait 5000
perf stop
mark lap-2
perf sample streaming-flythrough/lap-3
route 1000 NW_CITY_MERCHANT_TRADE_04 NW_CITY_HABOUR_BENCH_01 NW_FOREST_PATH_16
